{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"USN-8075-1","published":"2026-03-04T17:42:21Z","modified":"2026-06-25T13:32:31.668351093Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2025-10934","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-14422","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-2760","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-48797","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-48798"],"upstream":["UBUNTU-CVE-2025-2760","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-10934","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-14422","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-48797","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-48798"],"summary":"gimp vulnerabilities","details":"Michael Randrianantenaina discovered that calculating the linear size of a\nDDS file could overflow on 32-bit systems. An attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. This\nissue only affected Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 24.04\nLTS. (CVE-2025-2760)\n\nMichael Randrianantenaina discovered that GIMP did not perform any bounds\nchecking when calculating an offset into XWD Colormaps. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2025-10934)\n\nIt was discovered that GIMP's PNM loader did not sufficiently check that\nthe image could fit within the allocated memory, which could cause GIMP to\nread or write out-of-bounds. An attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-14422)\n\nIt was discovered that maliciously-crafted TGA files could cause memory\ncorruption and leave GIMP in an inconsistent state. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2025-48797)\n\nIt was discovered that a maliciously-crafted XCF file could cause GIMP to\nfree the same memory region twice, or access an already freed address. An\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or\nexecute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-48798)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"gimp","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/gimp?arch=source&distro=esm-apps%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.8.16-1ubuntu1.1+esm2"}]}],"versions":["2.8.14-1ubuntu2","2.8.14-1.2ubuntu1","2.8.16-1ubuntu1","2.8.16-1ubuntu1.1","2.8.16-1ubuntu1.1+esm1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"gimp","binary_version":"2.8.16-1ubuntu1.1+esm2"},{"binary_name":"gimp-data","binary_version":"2.8.16-1ubuntu1.1+esm2"},{"binary_name":"libgimp2.0","binary_version":"2.8.16-1ubuntu1.1+esm2"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2025-10934","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.0/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2025-14422","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.0/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2025-48797","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]},{"id":"CVE-2025-48798","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},{"score":"medium","type":"Ubuntu"}]}],"ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS"},"source":"https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices/blob/main/osv/usn/USN-8075-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"gimp","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:18.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/gimp?arch=source&distro=esm-apps%2Fbionic"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.8.22-1ubuntu0.1~esm2"}]}],"versions":["2.8.20-1","2.8.20-1.1","2.8.20-2","2.8.22-1","2.8.22-1ubuntu0.1~esm1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"gimp","binary_version":"2.8.22-1ubuntu0.1~esm2"},{"binary_name":"gimp-data","binary_version":"2.8.22-1ubuntu0.1~esm2"},{"binary_name":"libgimp2.0","binary_version":"2.8.22-1ubuntu0.1~esm2"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2025-10934","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.0/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","type":"CVSS_V3"},